===========================================================
STANDARD CALCULATOR SOLAR PANEL — TECHNICAL DETAILS
===========================================================

TYPE:
  • Polycrystalline or monocrystalline silicon photovoltaic strip
  • Typically 4–6 cells wired in series
  • Encapsulated in epoxy or acrylic “jewel” window

ELECTRICAL CHARACTERISTICS:
  • Open‑circuit voltage (Voc): 1.5 V – 3.0 V (bright indoor light)
  • Short‑circuit current (Isc): 20 µA – 200 µA (varies by size)
  • Maximum power: ~30 µW – 300 µW (typical calculator range)
  • Two terminals only:
        - Positive bus bar
        - Negative bus bar

PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTICS:
  • Thickness: 1–2 mm (including encapsulation)
  • Width: 10–20 mm (common)
  • Length: 20–60 mm (common)
  • Front surface:
        - Dark silicon cells
        - Silver bus bars visible as thin horizontal lines
  • Back surface:
        - Epoxy or plastic backing
        - Sometimes faint metal traces or frame

CONNECTION POINTS:
  • Pads may be hidden under epoxy
  • Any exposed bus bar or metal frame can be used as a contact
  • Conductive clamp or strap works if pads are inaccessible

OPERATING NOTES:
  • Works under ambient indoor light
  • Output rises significantly under direct sunlight
  • Ideal for ultra‑low‑power CMOS circuits (oscillators, charge pumps)
  • Perfect match for passive or semi‑active capacitive stylus designs

WHY IT WORKS FOR YOUR STYLUS:
  • Provides enough voltage to run a micro‑power oscillator
  • Lightweight and thin for stylus integration
  • Acts as a large conductive surface when tied to the metal core
  • No battery required — fully ambient‑light powered

===========================================================
END OF SOLAR PANEL DETAILS
